PRACTICAL – 4
Title:

Dynamic Analysis of Mobile Application using MobSF

Aim:

To perform dynamic analysis of an Android application using Mobile Security Framework (MobSF).

Objectives:
To understand dynamic analysis of Android applications
To deploy MobSF using Docker
To monitor application behavior during execution
To analyze runtime activities such as network communication and API calls
To identify runtime vulnerabilities in Android applications
Procedure:
(i) Install Docker

Open terminal and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install docker.io docker-compose -y

Start Docker service:

sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

Verify installation:

docker --version
(ii) Download and Configure MobSF

Clone MobSF repository:

git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/MobSF/Mobile-Security-Framework-MobSF.git

Navigate into directory:

cd Mobile-Security-Framework-MobSF

Run MobSF using Docker:

sudo docker-compose up
(iii) Open MobSF Dashboard

Open browser and visit:

http://127.0.0.1:8000
(iv) Start Android Emulator

Launch Android Virtual Device (AVD) from Android Studio.

Verify emulator connection:

adb devices
(v) Install DIVA APK on Emulator
adb install DivaApplication.apk
(vi) Upload APK to MobSF
Click Upload & Analyze
Select DivaApplication.apk
(vii) Perform Dynamic Analysis
Start dynamic analysis from MobSF dashboard
Launch the application on emulator
Interact with application features

MobSF monitors:

Runtime behavior
API calls
Network traffic
File access
Log activity
(viii) Observe Analysis Results

Review:

Runtime logs
Network requests
Application behavior
Security warnings and vulnerabilities
Observation:
MobSF successfully monitored application behavior during execution
Runtime activities and API calls were captured
Network communication and logs were analyzed
Dynamic analysis identified insecure runtime behavior and vulnerabilities
Result:

Dynamic analysis of the Android application was successfully performed using MobSF. Runtime behavior, network communication, and application interactions were monitored to identify potential security vulnerabilities.

Viva Questions:
Q: What is dynamic analysis?

👉 Analysis of application behavior during execution.

Q: Difference between static and dynamic analysis?

👉 Static analysis is done without running the application, while dynamic analysis is performed during runtime.

Q: What does MobSF monitor in dynamic analysis?

👉 API calls, logs, network traffic, runtime behavior, and file access.

Q: Why is dynamic analysis important?

👉 It helps detect runtime vulnerabilities that may not appear in static analysis.

